WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.815 --> 00:00:13.035
Will tried to protect his goldfish from Tish, the family cat.

2
00:00:13.055 --> 00:00:14.276
"Silly cat!

3
00:00:14.656 --> 00:00:17.277
Those fish aren't a snack, and I have to study!"

4
00:00:18.477 --> 00:00:20.858
He turned back to his science textbook and yawned.

5
00:00:20.878 --> 00:00:26.039
"This is boring," he murmured, pushing away his homework.

6
00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:29.100
"Isn't the ocean just water anyway?

7
00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:35.842
I'm so tired Will glanced at the time on his phone, set an alarm for ten minutes later,

8
00:00:36.222 --> 00:00:37.102
and crawled into bed.

9
00:00:37.822 --> 00:00:40.023
He immediately fell asleep and started to dream.

10
00:00:41.963 --> 00:00:45.484
Will found himself inside a submarine, floating in the middle of nowhere.

11
00:00:45.504 --> 00:00:48.165
"Wow! Where am I, QT?"

12
00:00:48.665 --> 00:00:49.926
he said, picking up his phone.

13
00:00:49.946 --> 00:00:56.708
"My GPS indicates that we're floating in the western Pacific Ocean," QT responded.

14
00:00:56.728 --> 00:00:59.936
"See?" "Wow.

15
00:01:00.456 --> 00:01:02.917
That's a lot of water," Will commented.

16
00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:12.099
"Almost three quarters of Earth is covered by water: the Pacific, Atlantic, Indian, Arctic, and Southern oceans.

17
00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:19.521
But they're connected into one world ocean because water moves all around," QT explained.

18
00:01:20.742 --> 00:01:22.942
Will peered at the map on QT's screen.

19
00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:25.463
"The continents seem so small."

20
00:01:25.483 --> 00:01:29.124
"They're bigger than they look," QT said.

21
00:01:30.024 --> 00:01:32.545
"Wait a second, and I'll take control of the ship."

22
00:01:33.305 --> 00:01:37.986
A beam of light shot from QT to the submarine's controls, and the ship began moving.

23
00:01:38.006 --> 00:01:39.787
"You can do that?

24
00:01:40.447 --> 00:01:42.168
Wow!" Will exclaimed.

25
00:01:42.188 --> 00:01:45.389
"I sure can.

26
00:01:46.069 --> 00:01:50.910
Right now we're over a strip around the continents called the continental shelf.

27
00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:55.351
It can extend four hundred kilometers from the coast.

28
00:01:55.752 --> 00:02:00.970
But it's not steep, so the water is usually 140 meters at its deepest."

29
00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:08.694
"Colorful tropical reefs and lots of animals live in this area," Will said, remembering something he had read

30
00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:09.435
in his textbook.

31
00:02:09.455 --> 00:02:12.537
"That's right," QT said.

32
00:02:12.557 --> 00:02:15.398
"Then the ground gets steeper.

33
00:02:15.798 --> 00:02:19.520
We call this section of the continents the continental slope.

34
00:02:19.961 --> 00:02:22.362
It goes all the way to the ocean floor."

35
00:02:23.402 --> 00:02:25.864
The submarine descended quickly, startling Will.

36
00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:27.808
"Where are we going?"

37
00:02:27.828 --> 00:02:31.670
"Down!" QT answered.

38
00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:33.771
"But I've got to turn on the lights.

39
00:02:34.471 --> 00:02:37.372
Sunlight doesn't penetrate very far into the water.

40
00:02:38.413 --> 00:02:44.075
The top layer of the ocean, the Sunlight Zone, is only two hundred meters deep.

41
00:02:45.176 --> 00:02:48.397
In this zone there's enough light for plants to survive.

42
00:02:48.877 --> 00:02:53.799
The fish and mammals that live here feed on the plants and—" "Each other?"

43
00:02:56.284 --> 00:02:56.544
Will guessed.

44
00:02:56.564 --> 00:03:03.629
"Right. As you go deeper, into the Twilight Zone, it grows dimmer and dimmer—not enough light for plants.

45
00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:09.533
So the creatures that live here usually have huge eyes to help them see.

46
00:03:10.894 --> 00:03:15.777
And they tend to come up to the Sunlight Zone to feed at night, when predators can't see

47
00:03:15.837 --> 00:03:17.398
them," QT explained.

48
00:03:17.418 --> 00:03:20.280
"That's where we are now, right?

49
00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:21.921
It's pretty dark here."

50
00:03:22.361 --> 00:03:25.023
Then Will noticed something enormous in the distance.

51
00:03:25.563 --> 00:03:26.124
"What's that?

52
00:03:26.588 --> 00:03:28.109
It's getting closer fast!"

53
00:03:28.129 --> 00:03:32.050
"Uh-oh That's a giant squid.

54
00:03:32.491 --> 00:03:35.312
They live here, feeding on fish and smaller squid.

55
00:03:35.752 --> 00:03:37.533
It probably thinks we're lunch!"

56
00:03:41.274 --> 00:03:46.616
Just as the giant squid was about to wrap its tentacles around the submarine, QT turned the boat

57
00:03:46.676 --> 00:03:48.057
sharply, and they sped away.

58
00:03:48.077 --> 00:03:51.138
"Whew!" said Will.

59
00:03:51.158 --> 00:03:58.654
"As I was saying," QT continued, "by one thousand meters deep, there's no light.

60
00:03:59.214 --> 00:04:01.395
That's the start of the Midnight Zone."

61
00:04:02.476 --> 00:04:03.076
Will nodded.

62
00:04:03.096 --> 00:04:04.477
"This must be it."

63
00:04:05.097 --> 00:04:06.918
Then he spied something surprising.

64
00:04:06.939 --> 00:04:12.402
"Lights!" "Many species have adapted to life without sunlight.

65
00:04:12.882 --> 00:04:17.865
Some create their own light, to attract mates or prey or confuse predators."

66
00:04:19.466 --> 00:04:23.068
QT turned off the lights, and a fish with huge teeth swam by.

67
00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:27.303
It had what looked like a fishing pole coming out of its head, with a light on the

68
00:04:27.343 --> 00:04:29.844
top. "That's weird!

69
00:04:30.365 --> 00:04:30.925
What is it?"

70
00:04:31.345 --> 00:04:31.886
Will asked.

71
00:04:31.906 --> 00:04:34.527
"An anglerfish.

72
00:04:35.048 --> 00:04:36.889
It attracts food with that light."

73
00:04:37.509 --> 00:04:40.751
After the fish swam away, QT flashed the submarine's lights.

74
00:04:41.392 --> 00:04:43.033
Thousands of lights flashed back.

75
00:04:43.974 --> 00:04:44.934
Will was amazed.

76
00:04:44.954 --> 00:04:48.356
"Wow! That's a lot of anglerfish!"

77
00:04:48.376 --> 00:04:53.440
"And some squid, some shrimplike species, and other creatures.

78
00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.281
We're approaching the ocean floor now.

79
00:04:57.641 --> 00:05:03.763
The ocean floor starts about four thousand meters below the surface, but it can go as deep as

80
00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:05.123
six thousand meters."

81
00:05:06.484 --> 00:05:09.945
QT turned the lights back on, and a vast plain appeared before them.

82
00:05:10.545 --> 00:05:11.765
It was dotted with mountains.

83
00:05:11.785 --> 00:05:20.248
"It looks a lot like the land above water; most of it is flat, but there are also

84
00:05:20.388 --> 00:05:21.528
mountains and valleys.

85
00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:25.341
Those little mountains are called seamounts.

86
00:05:25.941 --> 00:05:30.802
If they become big enough to reach the surface, their name changes to islands."

87
00:05:30.822 --> 00:05:34.123
"Cool!" Will exclaimed.

88
00:05:34.784 --> 00:05:36.064
Then he noticed something else.

89
00:05:36.084 --> 00:05:39.985
"What are those tubes, with the black stuff erupting out of them?"

90
00:05:42.146 --> 00:05:45.427
"They're called black smokers," QT said.

91
00:05:45.447 --> 00:05:50.208
"They release toxic gases and hot water from underground.

92
00:05:50.828 --> 00:05:55.370
For a long time, people thought nothing could live down here, but they were wrong."

93
00:05:56.771 --> 00:06:02.133
QT shined a bright light near one of the smokers, and they saw fish and crabs swimming among

94
00:06:02.173 --> 00:06:04.034
long, white tubes with red tips.

95
00:06:04.054 --> 00:06:07.075
"Those are tubeworms.

96
00:06:07.615 --> 00:06:11.157
They actually get their energy from those toxic substances.

97
00:06:11.517 --> 00:06:13.257
But let's look behind us too."

98
00:06:14.818 --> 00:06:17.799
As the submarine turned, the ocean floor dropped away.

99
00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:22.645
QT said, "That's the Mariana Trench, a huge valley.

100
00:06:23.525 --> 00:06:28.586
Its deepest part is the Challenger Deep, at 11,000 meters under the surface.

101
00:06:28.987 --> 00:06:30.927
But life exists even there.

102
00:06:31.327 --> 00:06:32.127
Let's go see."

103
00:06:33.888 --> 00:06:36.349
As they floated over the edge, they heard a creak.

104
00:06:37.049 --> 00:06:39.709
Worried, Will asked, "What was that?"

105
00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:45.251
QT ran a safety check of the submarine, and "DANGER!"

106
00:06:45.291 --> 00:06:46.671
appeared on the phone's screen.

107
00:06:47.772 --> 00:06:49.032
But QT sounded calm.

108
00:06:49.608 --> 00:06:51.269
"Our submarine made that noise.

109
00:06:51.809 --> 00:06:57.330
We are under extreme pressure down here, and the weight of all the water above us is pressing

110
00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:57.870
on the boat.

111
00:06:58.991 --> 00:07:00.411
We shouldn't go much deeper.

112
00:07:00.831 --> 00:07:06.913
We don't want to get squished and—" But before QT could finish, the submarine window cracked!

113
00:07:07.633 --> 00:07:10.414
A stream of water shot inside, splashing Will.

114
00:07:13.514 --> 00:07:18.096
He woke with a start and saw the cat jump away from the fishbowl, shaking its wet paw.

115
00:07:18.116 --> 00:07:20.970
"Tish! Stay away from that fishbowl!"

116
00:07:23.273 --> 00:07:24.254
Will went to his desk.

117
00:07:24.274 --> 00:07:26.097
"Oceans aren't boring.

118
00:07:26.717 --> 00:07:27.478
They're awesome!"

119
00:07:28.099 --> 00:07:30.182
he thought, quickly filling in a worksheet.

120
00:07:31.183 --> 00:07:34.868
Before long, he crawled back into bed—this time, for the night.
